config-connector-extensions patch 0049: mockgcp keeps a log sink's interceptChildren.

For logging.gcp.hfl.dev LoggingLogSink. The REST API's LogSink has
interceptChildren; the LogSink protobuf at cloud.google.com/go/logging
v1.18.0 (mockgcp's) has not, so the gRPC gateway dropped it. A new
mocklogging/sinkintercept.go, on the HTTP layer, keeps it beside each
sink, adds it to every sink it serves (get, list, create, update), and
refuses, as the API does, an intercepting sink that is not a folder's or
an organization's, whose includeChildren is not true, or whose
destination is not a Cloud project (logging.googleapis.com/projects/{id}).
An update naming interceptChildren in its mask may not change it (the API
has not been seen to; the kind keeps it immutable). Applies after 0029.
Upstream candidate: no, a stopgap until the protobuf has the field;
then the field belongs in logsink.go.

